    Adversarial lookahead hierarchy L0..L_inf: chain, derivative bound, first L2>L1 at n=6
    
    Prove L_r <= L_{r+1} <= F (information bound, one-ply split, monotone
    induction), the derivative bound L_r <= L0 + r, and pointwise finite
    convergence to the least fixed point L_inf of the one-ply operator.
    
    Exhaustive labelled-poset audit (A001035, 1/3/19/219/4231/130023):
    - n <= 5: L1 = L2 = F everywhere, no strict L2 > L1 (4473 posets).
    - n = 6: first 6480 strict L2 > L1 witnesses; smallest (0,0,0,1,3,27)
      e=30 L0/L1/L2 = 5/5/6, F=6; simplest 6-relation witness C2 u P4
      (0,0,0,1,6,22); deepest stabilization (48,0,0,0,0,0) e=240 needs five
      plies (L4=8 < 9=F=L5); L_inf = F for all n <= 6, r* = 5.
    
    Tests pin the n <= 5 exhaustive facts plus two explicit n = 6 witnesses
    under 5 s; the ~26 s n = 6 audit is excluded from CI.  Compare
    Stober-Weiss arXiv:2206.05597 (their Obs 2.2/2.3 are L0 <= F and
    L0 <= L1); no complexity, hardness, or running-time claim.

